{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"cat .pose/specs/2026-11-15-pose-strict-json-readers-require-the-end.md; cat .pose/rules/backend-go.md; cat pose-mcp/go.mod; cat pose-mcp/internal/cli/hook_runner_test.go; sed -n '990,1055p' pose-mcp/internal/mcpserver/server.go; rg -n 'json|EOF|strict' .pose/knowledge --glob '*.md'\"","aggregated_output":"---\nslug: pose-strict-json-readers-require-the-end\nstatus: in-progress\ncreated_at: 2026-11-15\ncompleted_at:        # stamped on the transition to status: done\nsupersedes:          # slug of the superseded spec (when applicable)\ndepends_on:          # prerequisites, inline list: other-spec, milestone:<roadmap>/<id>, roadmap:<slug>\nremediates: spec:pose-hooks-delegate-to-the-instance-runner@defect-fix\npriority:            # integer >= 0 (lower = higher priority); ordering preference, not a blocker\ncomponents: pose-mcp\ntask_type: bugfix\nsurface:             # optional: minimal | standard | full (default) — minimal drops Tasks and derivable report sections; `pose specs facts <slug>` derives them\ndelivers: capability:strict-json-readers-require-the-end\n---\n\n# Spec: pose-strict-json-readers-require-the-end\n\n## 1. Intent\n\n### Goal\nFazer todo leitor estrito de JSON do motor recusar conteúdo depois do valor que lê: um objeto válido seguido de lixo ou de um segundo valor é malformado, não lido como sua primeira parte.\n\n### Business value\nA revisão da spec `pose-hooks-delegate-to-the-instance-runner` (rodada 1, F1) achou que a policy de hooks, lida com `DisallowUnknownFields`, aceitava um objeto válido seguido de lixo e rodava o executor declarado. A mesma forma estava em outros dois leitores: a evidência de `pose release record` e o envelope de `pose action fulfil`. Os dois aceitavam conteúdo depois do objeto, e a evidência chegava a ser gravada como evento da release. Um leitor que se declara estrito e lê só o começo do arquivo aceita entradas que um leitor correto recusaria, e cada leitor novo podia repetir o erro, porque nada media a propriedade.\n\n### Constraints\n- Leitores que já exigem o fim (um segundo `Decode` comparado com `io.EOF`, `Token`, ou um `json.Unmarshal` dos mesmos bytes) não mudam.\n\n### Non-goals\n- Não tornar estrito um leitor deliberadamente permissivo (a policy de revisão aceita campos de motores mais novos).\n\n---\n\n## 2. Requirements\n\n### Functional\n- R1: The evidence of `pose release record`, the envelope of `pose action fulfil` and the hooks policy shall be refused when anything but white space follows their JSON value, and nothing shall be recorded or run.\n- R2: Every engine function that refuses unknown JSON fields shall also refuse content after the value, or name in the guard why the end need not be required.\n\n### Non-functional\n- Nenhuma.\n\n### Security\n- Fecha uma aceitação silenciosa de entrada malformada num leitor de evidência de release e num de envelope de ação.\n\n### Compatibility\n- Uma evidência, um envelope ou uma policy válidos, com ou sem espaço em volta, são lidos como antes.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Technical Plan\n\n### Affected areas\n- `pose/strict_json.go`: `DecodeStrictJSON`, um valor e nada depois.\n- `cli/release_lifecycle.go`, `cli/review_request.go`, `cli/maintenance.go`: os três leitores passam a usá-lo.\n- `pose/strict_json_test.go`: o teste do helper e o guard que percorre o fonte.\n\n### Artifacts\n- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/strict_json.go\n- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/strict_json_test.go\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/release_lifecycle.go\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_request.go\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/maintenance.go\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegated_review_request_test.go\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/release_review_regression_test.go\n- modified: .pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json\n\n### Delivery targets\n\n- capability:strict-json-readers-require-the-end module:pose-mcp profile:composed-capability entrypoint:pose-mcp/cmd/pose/main.go\n\nComposto em produção por `pose release record`, `pose action fulfil` e pelos git hooks do motor. Check permanente `strict-json-readers-require-the-end-integration`, evidenceClass `integration`, required: `go test ./internal/pose ./internal/cli -run 'TestDecodeStrictJSON|TestStrictJSONReadersRequireTheEnd|TestReviewRequestIsFulfilledOverTheCLI|TestF05RecordRefusesATagWhoseTreeIsNotIntact|TestAnInvalidHookRunnerIsRefused' -count=1`.\n\n### API/contract changes\n- Nenhuma: entradas válidas são lidas como antes.\n\n### Data/storage changes\n- Nenhuma.\n\n### Technical risks\n- Um arquivo que alguém escreveu com conteúdo extra depois do objeto passa a ser recusado; é o comportamento pretendido, e a mensagem diz o motivo.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Tasks\n\n### Implementation\n- [x] `DecodeStrictJSON` e os três leitores (R1).\n- [x] Guard pelo predicado real: funções com `DisallowUnknownFields` sem conferência do fim (R2).\n\n### Validation\n- [x] Regressões pela CLI para a evidência e o envelope, e o teste da policy de hooks.\n- [x] Prova de que o guard aponta os dois leitores originais sem a correção.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Decisions\n\n### Decision D1\n- Date: 2026-11-15\n- Context: sete leitores estritos já exigiam o fim de quatro formas diferentes, e três não exigiam.\n- Options considered: (a) corrigir só os três; (b) um helper comum e um guard que mede a propriedade no fonte.\n- Decision: (b).\n- Rationale: (a) deixava o próximo leitor livre para repetir o erro; o guard mede o predicado da regra (a mesma função que recusa campos desconhecidos exige o fim) e aceita as formas corretas que já existem, sem reescrevê-las.\n- Consequences: um leitor novo com `DisallowUnknownFields` usa o helper, confere o fim, ou declara no guard por que não precisa.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Validation\n\n### Strategy\nRegressão pela CLI de cada leitor corrigido, com lixo e com um segundo valor depois do objeto; teste do helper; guard sobre o fonte do motor, provado contra a árvore com o defeito.\n\n### Deterministic checks\n\n#### Test\n- Command: `go test ./internal/pose ./internal/cli ./internal/mcpserver ./internal/scaffold -count=1`\n- Scope: pose-mcp\n- Expected: verde\n\n### Execution log\n- Date: 2026-11-15\n- Environment: Linux, Go 1.26.\n- Notes: sem a correção, `pose action fulfil --envelope` aceitou um envelope seguido de lixo (`action.fulfil.preview=true`) e `pose release record` gravou a evidência seguida de lixo (`Recorded tagged for v1.0.0.`); o guard apontou `cmdReleaseRecord` e `cmdActionFulfil`. Com a correção, os três passam. A primeira versão do guard, que contava `io.EOF` por arquivo, deixou de ver os leitores que conferem o fim com um segundo `Decode`; o predicado foi corrigido para a função e para as formas que já existiam.\n\n### Results summary\n- Successes: as regressões reprovam sem a correção e passam com ela; o guard aponta os dois leitores originais e aceita os demais.\n- Failures: nenhuma.\n- Warnings: nenhum.\n\n### Requirement trace\n- R1 [satisfied] test:TestReviewRequestIsFulfilledOverTheCLI test:TestF05RecordRefusesATagWhoseTreeIsNotIntact test:TestAnInvalidHookRunnerIsRefused test:TestDecodeStrictJSONReadsOneValueAndNothingElse\n- R2 [satisfied] test:TestStrictJSONReadersRequireTheEnd check:strict-json-readers-require-the-end-integration\n\n### Known gaps\n- O guard reconhece `json.Unmarshal` na mesma função como conferência do fim, sem provar que é o mesmo conteúdo; nos dois casos atuais é.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Final Report\n\n### Delivered scope\n\nNão concluída.\n\n### Residual risks\n\n### Follow-ups\n# Rule: Backend Go\n\n## When to consult\n\nConsult this guide for HTTP handlers, domain services, persistence, concurrency, and integrations between Go services.\n\n## Required patterns\n\n- Handle and propagate errors with enough context for diagnosis.\n- Validate handler input and return HTTP status codes consistent with the contract.\n- Keep business rules in service or domain layers, not in transport code.\n- Honor `context.Context` for timeouts and cancellation.\n- Put data access behind clear interfaces that support testing.\n- Use structured logs without exposing sensitive data.\n\n## Blocking anti-patterns\n\n- Ignoring error returns, including `_` for critical errors.\n- Using `panic` in ordinary request flows instead of controlled error handling.\n- Coupling handlers directly to concrete repository implementations without an abstraction.\n- Running unbounded or unpaginated queries in potentially large endpoints.\n- Introducing concurrency without adequate synchronization or race protection.\n\n## Minimum checks\n\n- Run `go test ./...` in the affected scope.\n- Run `go test -race ./...` when concurrency changes.\n- Run `go vet ./...` without blocking findings.\n- Run the applicable Go lint check, such as `golangci-lint`, without critical errors.\n\n## Precedence in multi-domain conflicts\n\n- Apply the most restrictive security, contract, and operational rule when domain rules conflict.\n- Prefer verifiable check evidence and explicit risk mitigation when speed conflicts with control.\n- Record the precedence decision and objective rationale in the review.\n\n## Recurrence traceability\n\n> Also apply: [.pose/rules/_base-recurrence.md](_base-recurrence.md)\nmodule github.com/harne8/pose-mcp\n\ngo 1.26.0\n\nrequire (\n\tgithub.com/harne8/mcp-enforce v0.0.0\n\tgithub.com/redis/go-redis/v9 v9.22.0\n\tgithub.com/yuin/goldmark v1.8.4\n\tgo.opentelemetry.io/otel v1.47.0\n\tgo.opentelemetry.io/otel/exporters/otlp/otlpmetric/otlpmetrichttp v1.47.0\n\tgo.opentelemetry.io/otel/exporters/otlp/otlptrace/otlptracehttp v1.47.0\n\tgo.opentelemetry.io/otel/metric v1.47.0\n\tgo.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk v1.47.0\n\tgo.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/metric v1.47.0\n\tgo.opentelemetry.io/otel/trace v1.47.0\n\tgolang.org/x/sys v0.48.0\n)\n\nrequire (\n\tgithub.com/cenkalti/backoff/v5 v5.0.3 // indirect\n\tgithub.com/cespare/xxhash/v2 v2.3.0 // indirect\n\tgithub.com/go-logr/logr v1.4.4 // indirect\n\tgithub.com/go-logr/stdr v1.2.2 // indirect\n\tgithub.com/google/uuid v1.6.0 // indirect\n\tgithub.com/grpc-ecosystem/grpc-gateway/v2 v2.30.0 // indirect\n\tgo.opentelemetry.io/auto/sdk v1.2.1 // indirect\n\tgo.opentelemetry.io/otel/exporters/otlp/otlptrace v1.47.0 // indirect\n\tgo.opentelemetry.io/otel/log v1.47.0 // indirect\n\tgo.opentelemetry.io/proto/otlp v1.11.0 // indirect\n\tgo.uber.org/atomic v1.11.0 // indirect\n\tgolang.org/x/net v0.60.0 // indirect\n\tgolang.org/x/text v0.42.0 // indirect\n\tgoogle.golang.org/genproto/googleapis/api v0.0.0-20260928230214-8a89bd6388cc // indirect\n\tgoogle.golang.org/genproto/googleapis/rpc v0.0.0-20260928230214-8a89bd6388cc // indirect\n\tgoogle.golang.org/grpc v1.83.2 // indirect\n\tgoogle.golang.org/protobuf v1.36.12 // indirect\n)\n\nreplace github.com/harne8/mcp-enforce => ../mcp-enforce\npackage cli\n\nimport (\n\t\"bytes\"\n\t\"os\"\n\t\"path/filepath\"\n\t\"strings\"\n\t\"testing\"\n)\n\n// Spec pose-hooks-delegate-to-the-instance-runner.\nfunc hookRunnerRepo(t *testing.T, policy string) (string, string) {\n\tt.Helper()\n\troot := t.TempDir()\n\tartifactGit(t, root, \"init\", \"-q\")\n\tmarker := filepath.Join(t.TempDir(), \"ran\")\n\twriteArtifactTestFile(t, root, \"scripts/hook.sh\", \"#!/bin/sh\\nprintf '%s' \\\"$1\\\" > '\"+marker+\"'\\n[ \\\"$1\\\" = post-merge ] && exit 3\\nexit 0\\n\")\n\tif err := os.Chmod(filepath.Join(root, \"scripts/hook.sh\"), 0o755); err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n\t}\n\tif policy != \"\" {\n\t\twriteArtifactTestFile(t, root, \".pose/policy/hooks.json\", policy)\n\t}\n\tt.Chdir(root)\n\treturn root, marker\n}\n\n// R1: a declared runner gets the hook's name and its exit code is the hook's.\nfunc TestAHookDelegatesToTheDeclaredRunner(t *testing.T) {\n\t_, marker := hookRunnerRepo(t, `{\"schema_version\":1,\"runner\":\"scripts/hook.sh\"}`)\n\tvar out, errOut bytes.Buffer\n\tif code := HookMain(\"pre-commit\", &out, &errOut); code != 0 {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"pre-commit through the runner: %d %s\", code, errOut.String())\n\t}\n\tif got, _ := os.ReadFile(marker); string(got) != \"pre-commit\" {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"the runner was called with %q\", got)\n\t}\n\tif code := HookMain(\"post-merge\", &out, &errOut); code != 3 {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"the runner's exit code was not the hook's: %d\", code)\n\t}\n}\n\n// R2: a runner outside the project, not executable or under an unknown\n// schema is refused, and nothing runs.\nfunc TestAnInvalidHookRunnerIsRefused(t *testing.T) {\n\tfor name, policy := range map[string]string{\n\t\t\"outside\":        `{\"schema_version\":1,\"runner\":\"../hook.sh\"}`,\n\t\t\"absolute\":       `{\"schema_version\":1,\"runner\":\"/bin/true\"}`,\n\t\t\"missing\":        `{\"schema_version\":1,\"runner\":\"scripts/absent.sh\"}`,\n\t\t\"unknown schema\": `{\"schema_version\":2,\"runner\":\"scripts/hook.sh\"}`,\n\t\t\"unknown field\":  `{\"schema_version\":1,\"runner\":\"scripts/hook.sh\",\"shell\":true}`,\n\t\t\"trailing bytes\": `{\"schema_version\":1,\"runner\":\"scripts/hook.sh\"} garbage`,\n\t\t\"two objects\":    `{\"schema_version\":1,\"runner\":\"scripts/hook.sh\"}{\"schema_version\":1,\"runner\":\"scripts/hook.sh\"}`,\n\t\t\"not an object\":  `[{\"schema_version\":1,\"runner\":\"scripts/hook.sh\"}]`,\n\t} {\n\t\tt.Run(name, func(t *testing.T) {\n\t\t\t_, marker := hookRunnerRepo(t, policy)\n\t\t\tvar out, errOut bytes.Buffer\n\t\t\tif code := HookMain(\"pre-commit\", &out, &errOut); code != 1 || !strings.Contains(errOut.String(), \"hooks policy\") {\n\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"an invalid runner was not refused: %d %s\", code, errOut.String())\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tif _, err := os.Stat(marker); err == nil {\n\t\t\t\tt.Fatal(\"an invalid runner ran\")\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t})\n\t}\n}\n\n// R3: status names the runner a managed hook delegates to.\nfunc TestHookStatusNamesTheRunner(t *testing.T) {\n\troot, _ := hookRunnerRepo(t, `{\"schema_version\":1,\"runner\":\"scripts/hook.sh\"}`)\n\texe, err := os.Executable()\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n\t}\n\tif err := os.Symlink(exe, filepath.Join(root, \".git\", \"hooks\", \"pre-commit\")); err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n\t}\n\tvar out, errOut bytes.Buffer\n\tif code := cmdHooks(root, []string{\"status\"}, &out, &errOut); code != 0 || !strings.Contains(out.String(), \"delegates to \"+filepath.Join(root, \"scripts/hook.sh\")) {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"status: %d %s %s\", code, out.String(), errOut.String())\n\t}\n}\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn nil, err\n\t\t}\n\t\tevents, err := pose.LoadAmendments(pose.AmendmentsPath(spec.Path))\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"pose_spec_amendments: %v\", err)\n\t\t}\n\t\tadopted, err := store.ContractNodesAdopted()\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"pose_spec_amendments: %v\", err)\n\t\t}\n\t\tpending := pose.UnacknowledgedNodeChanges(spec.Slug, spec.Body, events, adopted)\n\t\tif events == nil {\n\t\t\tevents = []pose.Amendment{}\n\t\t}\n\t\tif pending == nil {\n\t\t\tpending = []string{}\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn map[string]any{\"slug\": spec.Slug, \"status\": spec.Status, \"events\": events, \"unacknowledged\": pending,\n\t\t\t\"contract_nodes\": pose.ProjectContractNodes(spec.Slug, spec.Body), \"capability_adopted\": adopted}, nil\n\tcase \"pose_list_specs\":\n\t\t// Arguments are decoded strictly and every value is validated before\n\t\t// the listing, as the CLI does: an unknown argument, an explicit zero\n\t\t// or an empty since would otherwise widen the result (spec\n\t\t// pose-cli-mcp-operation-results R3/R7).\n\t\tvar a struct {\n\t\t\tStatus     string  `json:\"status\"`\n\t\t\tComponents string  `json:\"components\"`\n\t\t\tCursor     string  `json:\"cursor\"`\n\t\t\tLimit      *int    `json:\"limit\"`\n\t\t\tRecent     *int    `json:\"recent\"`\n\t\t\tSort       string  `json:\"sort\"`\n\t\t\tSince      *string `json:\"since\"`\n\t\t\tProjectID  string  `json:\"project_id\"`\n\t\t}\n\t\tdecoder := json.NewDecoder(bytes.NewReader(args))\n\t\tdecoder.DisallowUnknownFields()\n\t\tif err := decoder.Decode(&a); err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"pose_list_specs: invalid arguments: %v\", err)\n\t\t}\n\t\tif err := requirePositiveLimit(\"pose_list_specs\", args); err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn nil, err\n\t\t}\n\t\t// An explicit null is a value, not an omission: decoding would turn\n\t\t// it into \"no filter\" and widen the listing.\n\t\tvar present map[string]json.RawMessage\n\t\t_ = json.Unmarshal(args, &present)\n\t\tfor key, raw := range present {\n\t\t\tif key != \"project_id\" && strings.TrimSpace(string(raw)) == \"null\" {\n\t\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"pose_list_specs: %s must not be null; omit it instead\", key)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t\tif _, given := present[\"sort\"]; given && a.Sort != \"date\" && a.Sort != \"slug\" {\n\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"pose_list_specs: sort must be \\\"date\\\" or \\\"slug\\\"\")\n\t\t}\n\t\tvar sinceDate time.Time\n\t\tif a.Since != nil {\n\t\t\tparsed, parseErr := pose.ParseSinceDate(*a.Since)\n\t\t\tif parseErr != nil {\n\t\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"pose_list_specs: %w\", parseErr)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tsinceDate = parsed\n\t\t}\n\t\trecent, limit := 0, 0\n\t\tif a.Recent != nil {\n\t\t\tif *a.Recent <= 0 {\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-27-handoff-delegation-mcp-round5.md:14:    - pose delegate ls --json\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-27-handoff-delegation-mcp-round5.md:15:    - pose validate --strict\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-27-handoff-delegation-mcp-round5.md:23:Independent round 5 reviewed implementation f0514d01404e7bed0cfc602f2db065f3e0c6289e of spec pose-delegation-mcp. The maintainer-authorized reviewer agent:independent-gpt-6.1-sol-review declares Codex/OpenAI, another vendor than implementer Claude/Anthropic. Identity is declared; this instance uses unsigned attestations. Last reviewed: 2026-10-27. Native global strict validation passed 158/158 checks at that implementation head.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-27-handoff-delegation-mcp-round5.md:45:Spec: .pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-mcp.md. Consumed knowledge: knowledge:delegation-observation-round4, knowledge:delegation-routing-round3 and knowledge:delegated-rounds-legacy-status. Canonical validation: .pose/results/delivery-validation.json. Local probes, seven mutations and reports: .review-work/round5/ (deliberately untracked). Native bundle and attestation IDs are recorded in the spec Final Report after closeout.\n.pose/knowledge/archive/2026-09-24-handoff-multirepo-review-continuation.md:12:  commands: [\"pose review verify spec:pose-agent-project-context\", \"pose closeout-check roadmap:pose-multirepo-foundation\", \"pose validate --strict --module pose-mcp --json .pose/results/delivery-validation.json --report\"]\n.pose/knowledge/archive/2026-09-24-handoff-multirepo-review-continuation.md:29:four strict spec lints pass. The `pose-mcp` matrix passed 25/25. Agent context\n.pose/knowledge/archive/2026-09-24-handoff-multirepo-review-continuation.md:41:   the interval, while `artifact-check --strict` still attributes the exact\n.pose/knowledge/archive/2026-09-24-handoff-multirepo-review-continuation.md:43:3. Rerun the strict matrix and targeted surface check, reseal the agent spec,\n.pose/knowledge/archive/2026-07-19-handoff-contract-baseline-handoff.md:12:  commands: [\"go -C pose-mcp test ./... -count=1\", \"pose check --strict\", \"pose validate --strict --module pose-mcp --report\"]\n.pose/knowledge/archive/2026-07-19-handoff-contract-baseline-handoff.md:57:(hook pre-commit, `.mcp.json`, symlinks `.claude/skills`) sem mutar nada,\n.pose/knowledge/archive/2026-07-19-handoff-contract-baseline-handoff.md:142:forma explícita e distinta; ownership/criticality do `module-metadata.json`\n.pose/knowledge/archive/2026-07-19-handoff-contract-baseline-handoff.md:190:- Popular `compatibility.json.supported_upgrades` com a primeira entrada\n.pose/knowledge/archive/2026-07-19-handoff-contract-baseline-handoff.md:204:  `internal/version.Version`; `server.json`, README quickstart e docs de CI\n.pose/knowledge/archive/2026-07-19-handoff-contract-baseline-handoff.md:207:  (`internal/mcpserver/testdata/tool-catalog.golden.json`) com risk classes e\n.pose/knowledge/archive/2026-07-19-handoff-contract-baseline-handoff.md:213:- Dogfood ativo: ownership em `module-metadata.json`, job `governance` no CI,\n.pose/knowledge/archive/2026-07-19-handoff-contract-baseline-handoff.md:228:  `supported_upgrades` no `compatibility.json` com pin SHA-256.\n.pose/knowledge/archive/2026-07-19-handoff-contract-baseline-handoff.md:240:- Confirmar o primeiro run de `mkdocs build --strict` (`docs.yml`) contra\n.pose/knowledge/archive/2026-07-19-handoff-contract-baseline-handoff.md:247:- Ao popular `compatibility.json.supported_upgrades` com a primeira entrada\n.pose/knowledge/archive/2026-07-19-handoff-contract-baseline-handoff.md:251:- `dependsOn` em `module-metadata.json` ainda não foi semeado para os módulos\n.pose/knowledge/archive/2026-07-19-handoff-contract-baseline-handoff.md:269:- Publicação do `server.json` em registry externo ainda é manual até\n.pose/knowledge/archive/2026-08-13-decision-log-install-one-liner-safe-form.md:12:  commands: [go -C pose-mcp test ./... -count=1, pose check --strict, pose validate --tolerant --module pose-mcp]\n.pose/knowledge/archive/2026-08-13-decision-log-install-one-liner-safe-form.md:46:the scaffold pipeline depends on. Security precedence (most restrictive rule\n.pose/knowledge/archive/2026-08-13-decision-log-install-one-liner-safe-form.md:54:drift); full `go -C pose-mcp test ./... -count=1` green; `pose check --strict`\n.pose/knowledge/archive/2026-08-03-decision-log-project-agnostic-assessment-evidence.md:75:- Confirmar `pose check --strict`, `pose validate` e `knowledge-check --strict`\n.pose/knowledge/archive/2026-08-15-decision-log-self-referential-policy-template-contamination.md:20:Issue #17 (reported against pose-mcp/pose CLI 1.2.0): `.pose/policy/delivery.json`\n.pose/knowledge/archive/2026-08-15-decision-log-self-referential-policy-template-contamination.md:21:and `.pose/policy/artifacts.json` on a target project seeded by `pose install`/\n.pose/knowledge/archive/2026-08-15-decision-log-self-referential-policy-template-contamination.md:33:which listed `\"policy\"` with no per-file exception. `delivery.json`/\n.pose/knowledge/archive/2026-08-15-decision-log-self-referential-policy-template-contamination.md:34:`artifacts.json` are pose-dist's own dogfooding config (adopted 2026-08-03/04,\n.pose/knowledge/archive/2026-08-15-decision-log-self-referential-policy-template-contamination.md:54:  distpolicy.go`) excludes `delivery.json`/`artifacts.json` from the wholesale\n.pose/knowledge/archive/2026-08-15-decision-log-self-referential-policy-template-contamination.md:65:- `pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/.pose/policy/{delivery,artifacts}.json`\n.pose/knowledge/archive/2026-08-15-decision-log-self-referential-policy-template-contamination.md:96:- `pose check --strict` at release-closeout time, once this change is\n.pose/knowledge/archive/2026-08-15-decision-log-self-referential-policy-template-contamination.md:99:  `artifact-check`, `pose report`, `pose validate --json`, in that order).\n.pose/knowledge/archive/2026-08-15-decision-log-self-referential-policy-template-contamination.md:131:  `pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/.pose/policy/{delivery,artifacts}.json`,\n.pose/knowledge/archive/2026-08-13-handoff-pr15-component-aware-review-provenance.md:12:  commands: [\"pose validate --strict --module pose-mcp\", \"pose review-check spec:pose-component-aware-review-plans\", \"pose artifact-check --spec pose-component-aware-review-plans --strict\", \"pose surface-check --spec pose-component-aware-review-plans --strict\"]\n.pose/knowledge/archive/2026-08-13-handoff-pr15-component-aware-review-provenance.md:40:- `pose validate --strict --module pose-mcp` passes all four matrix checks;\n.pose/knowledge/archive/2026-08-13-handoff-pr15-component-aware-review-provenance.md:41:  `artifact-check --strict` has zero errors and `surface-check --strict` has\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-24-decision-log-action-recovery-intent-and-refusal.md:22:Use one immutable intent per predecessor and the existing nonblocking journal lock. A command refuses without recording an action event; previews never sign. Keep incomplete operations visible and restrictive. Reference the prospective ADR for protocol and compatibility.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-11-02-handoff-agency-readiness-outcome-review.md:12:  commands: [\"pose review verify roadmap:agency-readiness\", \"pose knowledge-check --strict\"]\n.pose/knowledge/2026-11-02-handoff-agency-readiness-outcome-review.md:32:authorized answer, replay, closeout restriction removal and return after subject\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-26-handoff-delegation-routing-round3.md:25:F08: internal/cli/delegate.go computes independent_of_lead using vendor inequality alone. Configure a schema-2 agent with vendor unknown, model unknown, cli sh and read command [sh]. Both `pose delegate agents --lead anthropic/opus --json` and its text form disclose independent_of_lead=true. The correct conservative result is false or explicitly unknown. The auto router, achieved independence and run-backed authority do not consume this boolean. Acceptance is limited to this disclosure defect, not permission to credit unknown identities with independence.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-18-handoff-pose-b06-source-coverage-closeout.md:12:  commands: [\"pose review verify spec:pose-source-coverage-integrity\", \"pose close spec:pose-source-coverage-integrity\", \"pose check --strict\"]\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-18-handoff-pose-b06-source-coverage-closeout.md:53:[evidência compacta](../results/b06-independent-review.json).\n.pose/knowledge/2026-08-13-decision-log-adr-sealed-review-bundles-review.md:12:  commands: [\"pose lint-spec pose-review-bundle-convergence --ready-check\", \"pose validate --strict --module pose-mcp --report --report-task review-bundle-convergence\"]\n.pose/knowledge/2026-08-13-decision-log-adr-sealed-review-bundles-review.md:44:  historical evidence must be regenerated to recover the strict gate.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-08-16-decision-log-module-metadata-discovery-invalidates-review-provenance.md:25:and added it to `.pose/indexes/module-metadata.json`. That single addition\n.pose/knowledge/2026-08-16-decision-log-module-metadata-discovery-invalidates-review-provenance.md:30:spec whose scope touches `module-metadata.json`: between 3 and 22 specs\n.pose/knowledge/2026-08-16-decision-log-module-metadata-discovery-invalidates-review-provenance.md:70:  `module-metadata.json`, per `pose-gate-closeout-procedure` — this is\n.pose/knowledge/2026-11-04-handoff-pose-b34-implementation.md:13:    - \"go -C pose-mcp test -json ./... -count=1 -timeout=10m\"\n.pose/knowledge/2026-11-04-handoff-pose-b34-implementation.md:14:    - \"pose lint-spec pose-governance-read-view-generation --strict\"\n.pose/knowledge/2026-11-04-handoff-pose-b34-implementation.md:120:- [Start atual](../starts/pose-governance-read-view-generation.json)\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-20-handoff-pose-b07-implementation.md:12:  commands: [\"pose validate --strict --module pose-mcp\", \"pose check --strict\", \"go test -race ./internal/pose ./internal/cli ./internal/mcpserver\"]\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-20-handoff-pose-b07-implementation.md:29:`../results/b07-validation.json`.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-20-handoff-pose-b07-implementation.md:34:2. The unused expired Actions waiver was removed separately in d957b4f. No pin or enforcement change. Reconciled full suite, 11/11 mutations and native 141/141 validation passed before the latest three review fixes; regenerate final evidence at the configured .pose/results/delivery-validation.json.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-08-14-decision-log-escalation-validate-native.md:12:  commands: [\"pose recurrence-check --tolerant --window-days 30 --threshold 3\", \"pose stats workflows --since-days 30\", \"pose stats tasks --since-days 30 --json\", \"pose validate --strict --module pose-mcp --json .pose/results/delivery-validation.json --report\"]\n.pose/knowledge/2026-08-14-decision-log-escalation-validate-native.md:26:strict PASS on the same day, so they are not uncovered incidents.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-08-14-decision-log-escalation-validate-native.md:34:`.pose/reports/history/interventions.jsonl`; the historical failures remain\n.pose/knowledge/2026-08-14-decision-log-escalation-validate-native.md:64:- `.pose/reports/history/standard-validate-native.jsonl`\n.pose/knowledge/2026-08-14-decision-log-escalation-validate-native.md:65:- `.pose/reports/history/standard-test-plan-baseline-pose-mcp-active-context.jsonl`\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-27-handoff-delegated-rounds-legacy-status.md:13:    - pose review status --json\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-27-handoff-delegated-rounds-legacy-status.md:14:    - pose delegate ls --json\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-27-handoff-delegated-rounds-legacy-status.md:29:The independent composed-handoff fixture produced a native interrupted run with Round=1. Before handing it off, pose review status --json returned an interrupted_runs row with no round field, while the recorded run had Round=1. The same fixture then handed off and continued the handoff-owned session successfully in round 2. Local reproduction and output: .review-work/round4/handoff-probe.txt and handoff-probe.log (deliberately untracked).\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-27-handoff-delegated-rounds-legacy-status.md:33:Reproduce with the existing run-continuity fixture or a fake agent that captures a synthetic session and exits with declared limit code 75. Compare the persisted run, pose delegate ls --json, and pose review status --json before resume. Add regression coverage that the legacy summary/text reports the round and relevant lineage, or explicitly document its narrower legacy projection before retirement. Run the continuity, delegation and round suites. Review by 2026-11-26 or before removing the deprecated alias.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-28-handoff-delegated-conclusions-round4.md:28:The Unix backend propagates flock errors unchanged. A synthetic overlay returning syscall.EOPNOTSUPP, with only the wait bound reduced from two minutes to 200 ms, reached the deadline in 201 ms and reported another conclusion holding the lock. It published zero proofs and attestations. This is injected error-path evidence, not a claim that the local filesystem lacks flock. Evidence: .review-work/round4/permanent.log, permanent-overlay.json, permanent_lock.go and permanent_wait.go (local, untracked).\n.pose/knowledge/2026-11-02-handoff-roadmap-v7-independent-outcomes-20261102.md:12:  commands: [\"pose roadmap-check pose-v7-onboarding-and-consolidation --strict\", \"bash tests/journeys/install-and-upgrade.sh --binary <HEAD CLI>\", \"bash tests/quickstart/first-governed-loop.sh --binary <HEAD CLI>\"]\n.pose/knowledge/2026-11-02-handoff-roadmap-v7-independent-outcomes-20261102.md:24:Fresh CLI build, focused CLI/signature/MCP/presence tests, all quickstart chapters and install/6.2.0-upgrade journeys pass. Supplied strict validation has 184 passing checks at HEAD; full matrix was inspected, not rerun. All three prose milestone gates and their current dependency order were independently reviewed.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-14-decision-log-adr-shared-worktree-runtime-review.md:12:  commands: [\"pose lint-spec pose-consolidation-batch-14-authoring --strict\"]\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-14-decision-log-adr-release-temporal-evidence-review.md:12:  commands: [\"pose lint-spec pose-consolidation-batch-13-authoring --strict\"]\n.pose/knowledge/2026-09-12-note-cli-output-design-taxonomy.md:12:  commands: [\"pose check --strict\", \"pose knowledge-check --strict\", \"pose specs --json\", \"pose followups --json\", \"pose usage --json\", \"pose doctor --json\", \"pose review-plan spec:<slug> --json\", \"pose artifact-check --spec <slug> --json\", \"pose check --json\", \"pose lint-spec <slug> --json\", \"pose history-check --json\", \"pose knowledge-check --json\", \"pose skills-check --json\", \"pose recurrence-check --json\", \"pose index --json\", \"pose state --json\"]\n.pose/knowledge/2026-09-12-note-cli-output-design-taxonomy.md:36:`pose check --strict` and `pose knowledge-check --strict` are the validation this\n.pose/knowledge/2026-09-12-note-cli-output-design-taxonomy.md:38:(which commands accept `--json`, and what they print).\n.pose/knowledge/2026-09-12-note-cli-output-design-taxonomy.md:48:half: a human channel that machines already parse, and a `--json` channel that\n.pose/knowledge/2026-09-12-note-cli-output-design-taxonomy.md:94:pose check --json          → Error: invalid argument: --json\n.pose/knowledge/2026-09-12-note-cli-output-design-taxonomy.md:95:pose lint-spec X --json    → Error: unknown option: --json\n.pose/knowledge/2026-09-12-note-cli-output-design-taxonomy.md:96:pose knowledge-check --json→ Usage: pose knowledge-check [--strict|--tolerant] …\n.pose/knowledge/2026-09-12-note-cli-output-design-taxonomy.md:97:pose specs --json          → (valid JSON on stdout)\n.pose/knowledge/2026-09-12-note-cli-output-design-taxonomy.md:101:**`--json` means two different things.** 55 parse sites. In most commands it is\n.pose/knowledge/2026-09-12-note-cli-output-design-taxonomy.md:118:| `.pose/results/*.json` (validation result) | each check's own captured `Output` (tail, secrets redacted), outcome, duration, exit code | only if we change what we capture from the child, not how we print |\n.pose/knowledge/2026-09-12-note-cli-output-design-taxonomy.md:120:| `.pose/reports/history/*.jsonl` | report metadata only (`reportRecord`: task, outcome, hash, change set…) — **no captured output** | no |\n.pose/knowledge/2026-09-12-note-cli-output-design-taxonomy.md:215:      … 3 more lines — full output in .pose/results/validate.json\n.pose/knowledge/2026-09-12-note-cli-output-design-taxonomy.md:276:  command's own failures to stderr, so `pose x --json | jq` is always safe;\n.pose/knowledge/2026-09-12-note-cli-output-design-taxonomy.md:307:*Today:* mixed. `--json` is boolean in most commands and a path in `validate`;\n.pose/knowledge/2026-09-12-note-cli-output-design-taxonomy.md:312:- `--json` means **JSON on stdout**, everywhere, for every command that has a\n.pose/knowledge/2026-09-12-note-cli-output-design-taxonomy.md:313:  result; `--json-out <path>` (plus the existing `--junit`, `--sarif`) writes a\n.pose/knowledge/2026-09-12-note-cli-output-design-taxonomy.md:314:  file. `validate`'s current `--json <path>` stays as a deprecated alias,\n.pose/knowledge/2026-09-12-note-cli-output-design-taxonomy.md:352:8. **Agents are first-class readers.** For them the plain profile plus `--json`\n.pose/knowledge/2026-09-12-note-cli-output-design-taxonomy.md:363:| 4 | Machine channel: `--json` on stdout everywhere, `--json-out` for files, `--quiet`, exit-code contract, gates that have no JSON get it, internal parsers move to structured input | Must land before or with the restyle of the lines they parse |\n.pose/knowledge/2026-09-12-note-cli-output-design-taxonomy.md:372:2. **`--json` semantics.** Standardise on stdout and demote `validate --json <path>`\n.pose/knowledge/2026-09-12-note-cli-output-design-taxonomy.md:385:  gates apply (`go test -count=1 ./...`, `pose check --strict`,\n.pose/knowledge/2026-09-12-note-cli-output-design-taxonomy.md:421:- `docs-site/docs/cli.md` — the reference that would document `--json`,\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
