{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_27","type":"agent_message","text":"decision: changes-requested\n\nOne medium blocker remains in R2’s regression guard. The three production readers correctly reject trailing content, and the focused regression suite passed.\n\n**F1 — medium, blocker:** [strict_json_test.go:95](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-3488747883/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/strict_json_test.go:95) treats `Decode(new(T))` as proof of an end check. A reader containing `DisallowUnknownFields(); return dec.Decode(new(Config))` therefore passes the guard while accepting trailing JSON. Lines 90–91 also accept `More()`, which returns false for trailing `}` or `]` without establishing EOF. Require a checked end condition and add negative fixtures for these cases.\n\nApplied the review workflow and backend-Go, security, documentation-style, and delivery-evidence rules. Reviewed bundle `rvb-86557565efa7bcaf` against R1, R2, and D1.\n\nThe artifact gate passed with 956 warnings and no blocking findings; the surface gate reported no findings. Full validation uses the sealed pipeline evidence. An additional in-memory probe could not compile because the sandbox refused Go’s build directory; F1 follows directly from the guard and the installed Go implementation. No repository files were changed or attestation recorded.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"changes-requested\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"F1\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/strict_json_test.go\",\n      \"line\": 95,\n      \"summary\": \"R2's guard accepts readers without an end-of-input check. The Decode(new(T)) branch sets ends=true even for a function whose only decode is return dec.Decode(new(Config)); that function refuses unknown fields but accepts content after its first value. The More branch at lines 90-91 is also unsound: after decoding an object, More returns false for trailing } or ], so a reader using if dec.More() to reject extra content still accepts malformed input. These are unlisted exceptions to R2, beyond the spec's documented json.Unmarshal approximation. Require a checked end condition associated with the reader, remove these standalone acceptance shortcuts, and add negative guard fixtures proving both defective readers are rejected.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assumption-integrity\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-a21e66eb8f038eb6\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Examined R1/R2, D1, every production DisallowUnknownFields site, and the documented Unmarshal approximation. Existing readers check the end or validate the same complete bytes; the MCP exception relies on parsed transport arguments. The new guard's broader assumption is unresolved and reported as F1, not accepted as a risk.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-concurrency\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The helper creates a decoder per call and introduces no shared mutable state, goroutines, cancellation changes, or lifecycle changes.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-contracts\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/strict-json-readers-require-the-end-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Valid inputs retain their schemas and command behavior. R1 explicitly requires refusing malformed suffixes; no CLI or MCP signatures changed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-input-errors\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/strict-json-readers-require-the-end-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The helper rejects unknown fields, malformed input, second values and trailing garbage. Callers return before recording or executing; focused regressions passed locally.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-integration-impact\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/strict-json-readers-require-the-end-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Inspected all three production call sites and their consumers. Release recording, action fulfilment and hooks use the shared helper before side effects.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-observability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Trailing-content errors are bounded and do not echo payloads. Hooks retain policy-path context, release recording returns the parse error, and action fulfilment retains its established envelope diagnostic.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"compatibility\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/strict-json-readers-require-the-end-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Examined caller diffs and positive controls. Valid JSON with surrounding whitespace remains accepted; refusing appended content is the intentional R1 compatibility change. Deliberately permissive readers remain untouched.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"correctness\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"F1\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"design-causality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"F1\",\n      \"rationale\": \"D1's shared helper addresses the single-decode root cause correctly, but the guard does not establish the property D1 and R2 require.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"documentation\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-a21e66eb8f038eb6\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Examined the spec, helper comments and validation-matrix entry. Production behavior matches R1, the new integration command names existing tests, and no operational command syntax or scaffold changed. R2's implementation gap is recorded as F1.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"operability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/strict-json-readers-require-the-end-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Reviewed rejection paths and diagnostics. Malformed files fail before effects and return actionable parse or envelope errors; correcting the input permits the existing successful flow.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"requirements\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"F1\",\n      \"rationale\": \"R1 is supported by the helper tests and passing caller regressions. R2 is incomplete because defective readers can satisfy the new guard without a reasoned exception.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"scope\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-a21e66eb8f038eb6\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Compared the complete range with the spec's artifact declarations and delivery target. Runtime changes are confined to the helper and three specified readers, with regression tests and governance records.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"security\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/strict-json-readers-require-the-end-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Inspected validation ordering, existing path confinement and side-effect boundaries. Malformed suffixes cannot reach release publication, fulfilment recording or hook execution. No new dependencies, credentials or authority paths were introduced.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"solution-proportionality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-a21e66eb8f038eb6\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Compared D1's helper and guard with three duplicated EOF checks. The small shared helper removes repetition without dependencies or speculative abstractions. A bounded guard is proportionate, subject to fixing F1; requiring a full semantic analyzer would exceed this scope. Intentional multi-value input contracts would invalidate the helper's applicability.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"artifact-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-strict-json-readers-require-the-end --strict\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Executed with JSON output for inspection: exit 0, 956 warnings and no error or critical findings. Also inspected the explicit requested Git range.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-design\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-a21e66eb8f038eb6\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Used the sealed structural evidence and independently inspected R1/R2, D1 and the source. Did not regenerate assessment artifacts under the read-only boundary.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-discover\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Component discovery was unnecessary for this bounded reader change; inspected the affected module directly without writing assessment artifacts.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-integrate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"rationale\": \"No inter-module API or MCP contract changed. Inspected caller composition and existing strict readers, and used the sealed integration evidence without regenerating assessments.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-tech-debt\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Did not write an assessment. Inspected the changed source for debt markers and reviewed the spec's known gap; no new debt markers were introduced.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"closeout-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Requires the completed, recorded review conclusion. No attestation is recorded by this review, and F1 remains open.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"review-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Cannot verify this review before POSE records its conclusion.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"suggest-review\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Executed and applied the selected review workflow, security, documentation-style and backend-Go rules.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"surface-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/strict-json-readers-require-the-end-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Executed pose surface-check --spec pose-strict-json-readers-require-the-end --strict: one target, 224 validation results and zero findings.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Inspected the sealed strict pipeline validation in .pose/results/delivery-validation.json: 224 passing checks. Used that execution rather than rerunning a validation producer under the read-only boundary.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/strict-json-readers-require-the-end-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Used the sealed module validation and independently reran the exact focused integration test pattern across internal/pose and internal/cli; both packages passed. The full validation producer was not rerun locally.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```"}}
